         answer='It meets all four points. (1) Connection to the kitchen: the oval table (0.915 × 1.83 m) stands in the same room as the kitchen units, about 1–3 m from the worktops. (2) Access outside: three 1.83 m sliding glass doors lead from the room onto the open area between the two ground-floor flats. That area is not modelled as a space, so whether it is a private terrace cannot be read from the model. (3) Orientation, taking +Y as north: the west flat\'s room is glazed on its west façade and opens east, and the east flat\'s room opens west through its sliding doors, so both get west light. (4) Capacity: four chairs per table, the minimum of four places.',
